LIVE on Cloud Run. All three mandatory requirements now met.

https://abyssal-7517955252.us-central1.run.app  revision abyssal-00002-mcj

  Gemini 3.5+              YES, live on every data stage
  Google agent framework   YES, ADK LlmAgent + InMemoryRunner
  Google Cloud service     YES, Cloud Run

CONTAINER, corrected against a suggested Dockerfile that would not have started:
  CMD web.app:app, not app.main:app. The suggested version pointed at a package
  this project does not have; that container starts, fails and restarts forever
  while the deploy reports success. Now asserted by a test AND by a build-time
  import smoke test, so the BUILD fails instead.
  python:3.13-slim to match the interpreter the suite was verified on.
  No build-essential: the envelope uses stdlib wave, so a toolchain would add
  hundreds of megabytes and a compiler to a public image for nothing.
  requirements-web.txt only. scripts/import_graph.py exercises every route in a
  fresh interpreter and proves the console reaches no google-adk, no pymupdf,
  no numpy. Installing the full requirements.txt would have put the whole agent
  framework on a public unauthenticated surface.
  .dockerignore and .gcloudignore, non-root user.

DEPLOY, closing two omissions adversarial review caught on the last project:
  --service-account with a dedicated account holding NO IAM roles. Without it
  the revision runs as project EDITOR, mintable from the metadata server on a
  PUBLIC url.
  --max-instances 3, which IS the spend cap.
  LASTEXITCODE checked, because ErrorActionPreference does not stop a failed
  native command and a broken build would report as a successful deploy.
  No GOOGLE_API_KEY on the service. The console is keyless and spendless.

TWO BUGS FOUND BY DEPLOYING RATHER THAN BY READING:

1. deploy.ps1 did not anchor its working directory, so PowerShell default cwd
   applied, --source . resolved to C:\Windows\System32, and gcloud spent two
   minutes uploading the Windows system directory before crashing on
   catroot2\edb.log. It also silently fell back to Buildpacks. A relative
   --source in a script that does not pin its location does not fail with
   "file not found"; it uploads your operating system. Fixed with
   Set-Location $PSScriptRoot plus a preflight that refuses to deploy if the
   required files are not in the cwd.

2. /healthz 404s on Cloud Run because THE GOOGLE FRONT END INTERCEPTS IT and
   serves its own 404. The request never reaches the container. Proved by
   comparing response bodies on the live url:
       /healthz      Google "That is an error" HTML     GFE
       /nope         our JSON error body                our app
       /health       our JSON error body                our app
       /api/healthz  our JSON error body                our app
   Renamed to /health. This also CORRECTS a wrong diagnosis on the previous
   project, where the identical 404 was blamed on a stale revision.
   Durable rule: a 404 is not evidence about your code until you have read the
   body and confirmed which server wrote it.

Verified live: /health, /, /api/run, /api/bands, /api/waveform and
/api/source-image all 200, with CSP, HSTS, nosniff and frame-deny present on
the public url.

73 tests plus 22 route assertions pass.
